From db8c0853263c1cb15ef6001d00fc81e5ffb8f0d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Egor 835 <egor.su.8@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 14:16:54 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] RadioInterfaceCapabilityController: Don't wait out the
 timeout on failure

Without a supported IRadioConfig HAL (devices with radio.config@1.0),
getHalDeviceCapabilities() replies with a null result, so
setupCapabilities() returned without notifying and every
getCapabilities() call from a binder thread blocked for 2 seconds.
Settings > Network & internet makes several such calls on its main
thread and froze for ~8 seconds.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: Ic1d35237d9a643c81c90f9aabf12b18d96126a20
---
 .../internal/telephony/RadioInterfaceCapabilityController.java | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/RadioInterfaceCapabilityController.java b/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/RadioInterfaceCapabilityController.java
index e8ef142..61b3794 100644
--- a/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/RadioInterfaceCapabilityController.java
+++ b/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/RadioInterfaceCapabilityController.java
@@ -129,6 +129,9 @@ public class RadioInterfaceCapabilityController extends Handler {
                     }
                     if (ar.result == null) {
                         loge("setupRadioInterfaceCapabilities: ar.result is null");
+                        // Wake up getCapabilities() instead of letting it wait out its timeout,
+                        // e.g. when there is no supported IRadioConfig HAL (< 1.1).
+                        mLockRadioInterfaceCapabilities.notify();
                         return;
                     }
                     log("setupRadioInterfaceCapabilities: "
-- 
2.56.0

